Package: easypaper
Title: Automate Reproducible 'Quarto' Manuscripts Ready for Submission
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Daniel", "Sanchez-Garcia", email = "danielsangarci@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-0710-6292"))
Description: Creates and builds reproducible scientific manuscripts written
    in 'Quarto'. create_paper() writes a project that holds only the paper:
    its sections as separate files, its references and journal style as a
    'CSL' (Citation Style Language) file, the setup of the analysis and the
    data. The functions of the package then render it for any journal, check
    citations and cross-references before every render, export figures to
    PNG, JPEG and TIFF at 600 dpi, give the supplementary material a
    document and a bibliography of its own, and build the submission folder:
    the manuscript split for double-blind review, together with a data and
    code compendium ready for a data repository. Every render records the
    versions of the packages it used, 'easypaper' included, with 'renv', so
    the manuscript can be rebuilt years later. Every render also sets the
    scientific names of the reference list in italics, checking genera and
    species against the Global Biodiversity Information Facility ('GBIF')
    Backbone Taxonomy <doi:10.15468/39omei>; italicize_species() does the
    same for any other bibliography.
